        "description": "The names rows of the person's files (tools/live-namespace `live-namespace rows`, src/serve/rows.rs), as a session the engine keeps open and reaches only by calls. Each call is one operation of the store's Rows (get, get_many, held_record_with_version, list_page, ids, mutate, stamp, totals, search, place, order, changes, minted, wait_for_order: src/store/by_calls.rs), each atomic alone, and is answered as a file of bytes (session.byte_result), so a page of rows is never held to one message. tool:your-files is its caller (its invoke.records.runs). It holds the person's database login alone (own-rows-postgres-connection on descriptor 3), so its reach is the database's host, and tool:your-files holds the byte store's key alone.",
